"Internal Error ()\nciteturn7view0 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://doi.org/10.1145/3857809\",\"lineno\":null}); \nURL https://doi.org/10.1145/3857809 is not accessible via this tool.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nLibra: Succinct Zero-Knowledge Proofs with Optimal Prover Computation (https://eprint.iacr.org/2019/317)\nciteturn7view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://eprint.iacr.org/2019/317\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 70\nL0: # What a lovely hat\nL1: #### Is it made out of 【0†tin foil†iacr.org】?\nL2: \nL3: 【1†Cryptology ePrint Archive】\nL4: \nL5:   * 【2†Papers】 Updates from the last:\nL6:     * 【3†7 days】\nL7:     * 【4†31 days】\nL8:     * 【5†6 months】\nL9:     * 【6†365 days】\nL10:     * * * *\nL11: \nL12:     * 【7†Listing by year】\nL13:     * 【8†All papers】\nL14:     * 【9†Compact view】\nL15:     * 【10†Subscribe†www.iacr.org】\nL16:     * * * *\nL17: \nL18:     * 【11†How to cite】\nL19:     * * * *\nL20:     * 【12†Harvesting metadata】\nL21:   * 【2†Submissions】\nL22:     * 【13†Submit a paper】\nL23:     * 【14†Revise or withdraw a paper】\nL24:     * 【15†Acceptance and publishing conditions】\nL25: \nL26: 【16†Image: Search Button】\nL27: \nL28: [Input] [Button: Search ]\nL29: #### Paper 2019/317\nL30: \nL31: ### 【17†Libra: Succinct Zero-Knowledge Proofs with Optimal Prover Computation】\nL32: \nL33: Tiancheng Xie, Jiaheng Zhang, Yupeng Zhang, Charalampos Papamanthou, and Dawn Song\nL34: ##### Abstract\nL35: We present Libra, the first zero-knowledge proof system that has both optimal prover time and succinct proof size/verification time. In particular, if C is the size of the circuit being proved (i) the prover time is O(C) irrespective of the circuit type; (ii) the proof size and verification time are both O(d log C) for d-depth log-space uniform circuits (such as RAM programs).\nL36: In addition Libra features an one-time trusted setup that depends only on the size of the input to the circuit and not on the circuit logic. Underlying Libra is a new linear-time algorithm for the prover of the interactive proof protocol by Goldwasser, Kalai and Rothblum (also known as GKR protocol), as well as an efficient approach to turn the GKR protocol to zero-knowledge using small masking polynomials. Not only does Libra have excellent asymptotics, but it is also efficient in practice.\nL37: For example, our implementation shows that it takes 200 seconds to generate a proof for constructing a SHA2-based Merkle tree root on 256 leaves, outperforming all existing zero-knowledge proof systems. Proof size and verification time of Libra are also competitive.\nL38: Note: keep aligned as virgo\nL39: ##### Metadata\nL40: Available format(s)\nL41:     【17†PDF】\nL42: Category\nL43:     【18†Cryptographic protocols】\nL44: Publication info\nL45:     A minor revision of an IACR publication in CRYPTO 2019\nL46: Keywords\nL47:     【19†Zero knowledge proof】【20†interactive proof】【21†polynomial delegation】\nL48: Contact author(s)\nL49:     zhangyp @ tamu edu\nL50: jiaheng_zhang @ berkeley edu\nL51: niconiconi @ berkeley edu\nL52: History\nL53:     2021-11-20: last of 8 revisions\nL54:     2019-03-29: received\nL55:     【22†See all versions】\nL56: Short URL\nL57:     【23†https://ia.cr/2019/317†ia.cr】\nL58: License\nL59: 【24†CC BY†creativecommons.org】\nL60: BibTeX 【25†Image】Copy to clipboard\nL61: \nL62:     @misc{cryptoeprint:2019/317,\nL63:           author = {Tiancheng Xie and Jiaheng Zhang and Yupeng Zhang and Charalampos Papamanthou and Dawn Song},\nL64:           title = {Libra: Succinct Zero-Knowledge Proofs with Optimal Prover Computation},\nL65:           howpublished = {Cryptology {ePrint} Archive, Paper 2019/317},\nL66:           year = {2019},\nL67:           url = {https://eprint.iacr.org/2019/317}\nL68:     }\nL69: Note: In order to protect the privacy of readers, eprint.iacr.org does not use cookies or embedded third party content.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn7view2 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://github.com/Plonky3/Plonky3/releases/tag/p3-sumcheck-v0.8.0\",\"lineno\":null}); \nFailed to fetch https://github.com/Plonky3/Plonky3/releases/tag/p3-sumcheck-v0.8.0: Cache miss--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGitHub - Alisah-Ozcan/GPU-NTT: Welcome to the GPU-NTT-Optimization repository! We present cutting-edge algorithms and implementations for optimizing the Number Theoretic Transform (NTT) on Graphics Processing Units (GPUs). · GitHub (https://github.com/Alisah-Ozcan/GPU-NTT)\nciteturn7view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn6view0\",\"pattern\":\"License\"}); Total lines: 377\nL71:     * SUPPORT & SERVICES\nL72:       * 【14†Documentation†docs.github.com】\nL73:       * 【44†Customer support†support.github.com】\nL74:       * 【45†Community forum】\nL75:       * 【46†Trust center】\nL76:       * 【47†Partners】\nL77: \nL78: 【48†View all resources】\nL79: \nL80:   * Open Source\nL81: \nL82:     * COMMUNITY\nL83:       * 【49†GitHub SponsorsFund open source developers】\nL84:     * PROGRAMS\nL85:       * 【50†Security Lab†securitylab.github.com】\nL86:       * 【51†Maintainer Community†maintainers.github.com】\nL87:       * 【52†GitHub Stars†stars.github.com】\nL88:       * 【53†Archive Program†archiveprogram.github.com】\nL89: \nL90:     * REPOSITORIES\nL91:       * 【54†Topics】\nL92:       * 【55†Trending】\nL93:       * 【56†Collections】\nL94: \nL95:   * Enterprise\nL96: \nL97:     * ENTERPRISE SOLUTIONS\nL98:       * 【19†Enterprise platformAI-powered developer platform】\nL99:     * AVAILABLE ADD-ONS\nL100:       * 【10†GitHub Advanced SecurityEnterprise-grade security features】\nL101:       * 【57†Copilot for BusinessEnterprise-grade AI features】\nL102:       * 【58†Premium SupportEnterprise-grade 24/7 supp