History\nL184: \nL185: 38 Commits\nL186: ## Folders and files\nL187: \nL188: Name  | Name  | Last commit message  | Last commit date\nL189: --- | --- | --- | ---\nL190: 【85†benchmark】  | 【85†benchmark】  |    |\nL191: 【86†cmake】  | 【86†cmake】  |    |\nL192: 【87†example】  | 【87†example】  |    |\nL193: 【88†src】  | 【88†src】  |    |\nL194: 【89†.gitignore】  | 【89†.gitignore】  |    |\nL195: 【90†CMakeLists.txt】  | 【90†CMakeLists.txt】  |    |\nL196: 【91†LICENSE】  | 【91†LICENSE】  |    |\nL197: 【92†README.md】  | 【92†README.md】  |    |\nL198: ## Repository files navigation\nL199: \nL200:   *   * 【93†README】\nL201:   * 【93†Apache-2.0 license】\nL202: \nL203: More items\nL204: # GPU-NTT\nL205: \nL206: Welcome to the GPU-NTT-Optimization repository! We present cutting-edge algorithms and implementations for optimizing the Merge and 4-Step Number Theoretic Transforms (NTT) on GPUs. GPU-NTT automatically supports both 32-bit and 64-bit arithmetic via Barrett reduction; the older manual reduction selection is kept in the 【94†paper_version】 branch.\nL207: \nL208: The associated research paper: 【95†https://eprint.iacr.org/2023/1410†eprint.iacr.org】\nL209: FFT variant of GPU-NTT is available: 【96†https://github.com/Alisah-Ozcan/GPU-FFT】\nL210: ## Development\nL211: \nL212: ### Requirements\nL213: \nL214:   * 【97†CMake†cmake.org】 >=3.26\nL215:   * 【98†GCC†gcc.gnu.org】\nL216:   * 【99†CUDA Toolkit†developer.nvidia.com】\nL217: ### Build & Install\nL218: \nL219: Configure + build:\nL220: \nL221:     cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DCMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES=86\nL222:     cmake --build build --parallel\nL223: \nL224: Install:\nL225: \nL226:     cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DCMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES=86\nL227:     cmake --build build --parallel\nL228:     cmake --install build\nL229: \nL230: Notes:\nL231:   * If you install to a system location (default: `/usr/local`), you may need `sudo` or set `-DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/your/prefix`.\nL232:   * If you omit `-DCMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES=...`, GPU-NTT defaults to `80;86;89;90`.\nL233:   * If CMake cannot find `nvcc`, set `CUDACXX=/path/to/nvcc` or pass `-DCMAKE_CUDA_COMPILER=/path/to/nvcc`.\nL234:   * If you change compilers/toolchains, prefer a clean configure: `cmake --fresh -S . -B build`.\nL235: ### Compile Options\nL236: \nL237: GPU-NTT uses C++17/CUDA17 and applies per-configuration compile flags.\nL238: \nL239:   * Build type (single-config generators like Makefiles/Ninja): `-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release|Debug|RelWithDebInfo|MinSizeRel`\nL240:   * Optimization/debug defaults:\nL241:     * `Release`: `-O3 -DNDEBUG`\nL242:     * `RelWithDebInfo`: `-O3 -g -DNDEBUG`\nL243:     * `Debug`: `-g` (and CUDA adds line info)\nL244:   * Extra warnings: `-DGPUNTT_ENABLE_WARNINGS=ON`\nL245: Example:\nL246: \nL247:     cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=RelWithDebInfo -DGPUNTT_ENABLE_WARNINGS=ON\nL248:     cmake --build build --parallel\nL249: ### Testing & Benchmarking\nL250: #### Examples (CPU & GPU Merge / 4-Step)\nL251: \nL252: Choose one of the data types at the top of the example files:\nL253: \nL254:   * typedef Data32 TestDataType;\nL255:   * typedef Data64 TestDataType;\nL256: \nL257: Configure + build:\nL258: \nL259:     cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DCMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES=86 -DGPUNTT_BUILD_EXAMPLES=ON\nL260:     cmake --build build --parallel\nL261: Run CPU examples:\nL262: \nL263:     ./build/bin/example/cpu_4step_ntt_examples <RING_SIZE_IN_LOG 2> <BATCH_SIZE>\nL264:     ./build/bin/example/cpu_merge_ntt_examples <RING_SIZE_IN_LOG 2> <BATCH_SIZE>\nL265:     # Example: ./build/bin/example/cpu_merge_ntt_examples 15 1\nL266: Run GPU examples:\nL267: \nL268:     ./build/bin/example/gpu_4step_ntt_examples <RING_SIZE_IN_LOG 2> <BATCH_SIZE>\nL269:     ./build/bin/example/gpu_4step_intt_examples <RING_SIZE_IN_LOG 2> <BATCH_SIZE>\nL270:     ./build/bin/example/gpu_merge_ntt_examples <RING_SIZE_IN_LOG 2> <BATCH_SIZE>\nL271:     ./build/bin/example/gpu_merge_intt_examples <RING_SIZE_IN_LOG 2> <BATCH_SIZE>\nL272:     # Example: ./build/bin/example/gpu_merge_ntt_examples 12 1\nL273: #### Benchmarking GPU NTT\nL274: \nL275: Choose one of the data types at the top of the benchmark files:\nL276: \nL277:   * typedef Data32 BenchmarkDataType;\nL278:   * typedef Data64 BenchmarkDataType;\nL279: \nL280: Configure + build:\nL281: \nL282:     cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DCMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES=86 -DGPUNTT_BUILD_BENCHMARKS=ON\nL283:     cmake --build build --parallel\nL284: \nL285: Run benchmarks:\nL286: \nL287:     ./build/bin/benchmark/benchmark_4step_ntt --disable-blocking-kernel\nL288:     ./build/bin/benchmark/benchmark_merge_ntt --disable-blocking-kernel\nL289: ## Using GPU-NTT in a downstream CMake project\nL290: Make sure GPU-NTT is installed before integrating it into your project. The installed GPU-NTT library provides a set of config files that make it easy to integrate GPU-NTT into your own CMake project. In your CMakeLists.txt, simply add:\nL291: \nL292:     project(<your-project> LANGUAGES CXX CUDA)\nL293:     find_package(CUDAToolkit REQUIRED)\nL294:     # ...\nL295:     find_package(GPUNTT CONFIG REQUIRED)\nL296:     # ...\nL297:     target_link_libraries(<your-target> (PRIVATE|PUBLIC|INTERFACE) GPUNTT::ntt CUDA::cudart)\nL298:     # ...\nL299:     set_target_properties(<your-target> PROPERTIES CUDA_SEPARABLE_COMPILATION ON)\nL300:     # ...\nL301: ## How to Cite GPU-NTT\nL302: \nL303: Please use the below BibTeX, to cite GPU-NTT in academic papers.\nL304: \nL305:     `@misc{cryptoeprint:2023/1410,\nL306:           author = {Ali Şah Özcan and Erkay Savaş},\nL307:           title = {Two Algorithms for Fast GPU Implementation of NTT},\nL308:           howpublished = {Cryptology ePrint Archive, Paper 2023/1410},\nL309:           year = {2023},\nL310:           note = {\\url{https://eprint.iacr.org/2023/1410}},\nL311:           url = {https://eprint.iacr.org/2023/1410}\nL312:     }\nL313:     `\nL314: or\nL315: \nL316:     `@ARTICLE{11003946,\nL317:           author={Ozcan, Alisah and Javeed, Arsalan and Savas, Erkay},\nL318:           journal={IEEE Access},\nL319:           title={High-Performance Number Theoretic Transform on GPU Through radix2-CT and 4-Step Algorithms},\nL320:           year={2025},\nL321:           volume={13},\nL322:           number={},\nL323:           pages={87862-87883},\nL324:           keywords={Graphics processing units;Polynomials;Instruction sets;Parallel processing;Kernel;Optimization;Memory management;Transforms;Computational efficiency;Tensors;Graphical processing unit;homomorphic cryptography;hardware acceleration;number theoretic transform;polynomial arithmetic},\nL325:           doi={10.1109/ACCESS.2025.3570024}\nL326:     }\nL327:     `\nL328: ## License\nL329: \nL330: This project is licensed under the 【91†Apache License】. For more details, please refer to the License file.\nL331: \nL332: ## Contact\nL333: \nL334: If you have any questions or feedback, feel free to contact me:\nL335: \nL336:   * Email: alisah@sabanciuniv.edu\nL337:   * LinkedIn: 【100†Profile†www.linkedin.com】\nL338: \nL339: ## About\nL340: \nL341: Welcome to the GPU-NTT-Optimization repository! We present cutting-edge algorithms and implementations for optimizing the Number Theoretic Transform (NTT) on Graphics Processing Units (GPUs).\nL342: ### Topics\nL343: \nL344: 【71†discrete-fourier-transform】【72†fast-fourier-transform】【73†gpu】【74†gpu-acceleration】【75†gpu-computing】【76†ntt】【77†number-theoretic-transform】\nL345: \nL346: ### Resources\nL347: \nL348: 【78†Readme】\nL349: \nL350: 【79†Apache-2.0 license】\nL351: \nL352: 【80†Activity】\nL353: \nL354: ### Stars\nL355: \nL356: 55 stars\nL357: \nL358: ### Watchers\nL359: \nL360: 2 watching\nL361: \nL362: ### Forks\nL363: \nL364: 【81†20 forks】\nL365: \nL366: 【82†Report repository】\nL367: \nL368: ## Releases\nL369: \nL370: ## Packages\nL371: \nL372: ## Contributors\nL373: \nL374: ## Languages\nL375: \nL376: You can’t perform that action at this time.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGitHub - Terminus-IMRC/tensor-core-ntt: Number theoretic transform (NTT) implementation using Tensor Cores on NVIDIA GPU · GitHub (https://github.com/Terminus-IMRC/tensor-core-ntt)\nciteturn7view4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn6view1\",\"pattern\":\"License\"}); Total lines: 250\nL141: ### Resources\nL142: \nL143: 【70†Readme】\nL144: \nL145: ### Contributing\nL146: \nL147: 【71†Contributing】\nL148: \nL149: 【72†Activity】\nL150: \nL151: ### Stars\nL152: \nL153: 9 stars\nL154: \nL155: ### Watchers\nL156: \nL157: 0 watching\nL158: \nL159: ### Forks\nL160: \nL161: 【73†2 forks】\nL162: \nL163: 【74†Report repository】\nL164: \nL165: main\nL166: \nL167: 【75†Branches】【76†Tags】\nL168: \nL169: [Input: Go to file]\nL170: \nL171: Go to file\nL172: \nL173: Code\nL174: \nL175: Open more actions menu\nL176: \nL177: ## Latest commit\nL178: \nL179: \nL180: \nL181: ## History\nL182: \nL183: 8 Commits\nL184: ## Folders and files\nL185: \nL186: Name  | Name  | Last commit message  | Last commit date\nL187: --- | --- | --- | ---\nL188: 【77†.devcontainer/native】  | 【77†.devcontainer/native】  |    |\nL189: 【78†include/polyarith】  | 【78†include/polyarith】  |    |\nL190: 【79†tests】  | 【79†tests】  |    |\nL191: 【80†.clang-format】  | 【80†.clang-format】  |    |\nL192: 【81†.editorconfig】  | 【81†.editorconfig】  |    |\nL193: 【82†CONTRIBUTING.md】  | 【82†CONTRIBUTING.md】  |    |\nL194: 【83†README.md】  | 【83†README.md】  |    |\nL195: ## Repository files navigation\nL196: \nL197:   *   * 【84†README】\nL198:   * 【84†Contributing】\nL199: \nL200: More items\nL201: # 【62†`tensor-core-ntt`】\nL202: \nL203: This repository provides an improved implementation of the 【85†number theoretic transform (NTT)†en.wikipedia.org】 that leverages Tensor Cores on NVIDIA GPUs.\nL204: \nL205: NTT is a generalization of the 【86†fast Fourier transform (FFT)†en.wikipedia.org】 over modular integers, and it is used to perform convolutions and polynomial/multiple-precision arithmetic exactly, in contrast to FFT, which uses floating-point arithmetic and thus suffers from rounding errors.\nL206: Through careful analysis, we successfully removed the redundant operations in the previous Tensor Core-based NTT implementations. Along with efficient modular reduction algorithm, we achieved higher performance than the previous work in most settings.\nL207: See the paper by Y. Sugizaki and D. Takahashi titled \"Improved Implementation of Number Theoretic Transform on NVIDIA GPU with Tensor Cores\" (doi:【87†10.1145/3773656.3773673†doi.org】), which was accepted to 【88†SupercomputingAsia 2026 / International Conference on High Performance Computing in Asia-Pacific Region 2026 (SCA/HPCAsia 2026)†www.sca-hpcasia2026.jp】, for more details.\nL208: ## License and contribution\nL209: \nL210: For license and copyright notices, see the SPDX file tags in each file. Unless otherwise noted, files in this project are licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (SPDX short-form identifier: Apache-2.0) and copyrighted by the contributors.\nL211: \nL212: Everyone is encouraged to contribute to this project. See the 【82†CONTRIBUTING.md】 file for instructions.\nL213: \nL214: ## About\nL215: \nL216: Number theoretic transform (NTT) implementation using Tensor Cores on NVIDIA GPU\nL217: \nL218: ### Resources\nL219: \nL220: 【70†Readme】\nL221: ### Contributing\nL222: \nL223: 【71†Contributing】\nL224: \nL225: 【72†Activity】\nL226: \nL227: ### Stars\nL228: \nL229: 9 stars\nL230: \nL231: ### Watchers\nL232: \nL233: 0 watching\nL234: \nL235: ### Forks\nL236: \nL237: 【73†2 forks】\nL238: \nL239: 【74†Report repository】\nL240: \nL241: ## Releases\nL242: \nL243: ## Packages\nL244: \nL245: ## Contributors\nL246: \nL247: ## Languages\nL248: \nL249: You can’t perform that action at this time.\n----------------------------------------------------------------------